Z||000000||Racer 1||09-30-1999||05:27 PM||||Hello, Just wanted to see how many people have raced R/C cars here in the fiero Forum. Back about 9 years ago I got into R/C cars. Alongside working on my fiero both hobbies are fun. Bolink used to make a 1/10 scale lexan fiero body. I tried to get them to make me 2 of them which would be way cool. But they said I had to buy 10 bodies and each one would cost 20$. 200.00$ for ten of them If anyone is interested in pitching in for there bodies mabey we could all have a fiero r/c bodie. Just a thought I want a fiero body bad. heres all the cars I have <P>HPI RS4 Nitro Racer 1/10 4wd gas sedan<BR>Team Associated RC10B3 electric buggy<BR>Team Associated RC10T3 electric truck<BR>Team Associated RC10GT gas truck<BR>Bolink 1/10 pan car <BR>Soon to be RC10TC3<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||mwbackus||09-30-1999||08:02 PM||||I have never raced one in my Formula, but, I hear they are way fast off the line!  One of my concerns would be running over it accidently.  :-)||||reg||1
Z||000002||GREENDANO||09-30-1999||10:01 PM||||I have both the nitro USA and the electric USA monster trucks.  I also have a nitro tracker too.  I enjoy the gas trucks much more than the electric stuff.  (no batteries to die)  Fiero bodies hmmmm.???  I don't think they would look right on my truck chassis'.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||10
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||09-30-1999||10:02 PM||||I have been racing r/c cars for about 6 years now. Ever heard of the April Fools Classic in Salt Lake City? I took 1st there in stock truck about 3 years ago! I think Traxxas used to make a Fiero R/C car, but have never seen it.<P>I mostly race offroad and for fun I measured my T2 in distance jumping....I put in a 7 cell 2000 300+ battery and a 10x4 Maxtec with a 25 pinion and a 88 spur. I hit the ramp at about 50 mph (guessing) and I flew nice and flat the first time with only small amounts of throttle/brake to get it to land right side up. I think I measured 39 feet with a height of about 15 feet off a ramp about 4 feet long and about 3 feet at the lip. The second time.....well let's just say I had get a new body and shock towers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>There are some club members drag racing them now and they are hitting 70 mph in less than 2 seconds!!!<P>If you get enough people together I guess I will take one, maybe two.<P>My R/C cars:<BR>Team Associated World's car (retired it)<BR>Team Associated  B2, B3 (retired the B2)<BR>Team Associated T2<BR>Team Losi XX4 (won this in a race raffle, cost me 5 bucks....compared to about 280)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||09-30-1999||10:15 PM||||I have not raced in about 7 or 8 years. I did more on-road racing and at one time had one of the Traxxas GTP Fiero cars. Got started in 1/10 off road with a "stick" radio. Then moved to 1/12 on-road and 1/10 on-road. I ran a speedway track for two years, that was a blast! It was a paved tri-oval. 1/10 modified would fly at this place. I still have all my stuff in the barn- Futaba PCM's and even two of the great Magnum Senior radios. I could make anybody's radio "glitch" with those things! Oh, the memories. Oh, the money! I have a closet full of trophies and track record plaques. Just to be young and foolish (and single) again...||||reg||6
Z||000005||SN1PERVII||10-01-1999||12:08 AM||||   Yeah I used to race nothing major mind you. Mostly just race guys in the neighborhood for braging rights. It has been about a year and a half since I ran my truck. It was a Kyosho Outlaw Ultima Truck. It was pretty cool. I had really wanted the Double Dare but got talked out of it. Now I waste most of my money on my Kawasaki. Oh well winter is coming time to find a new project.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Racer 1||10-01-1999||03:48 AM||||Cool Cool. I just got a cheesy website of my own. It looks like crap but im new to making a webpage so bare with me! <A HREF="http://fierorob.homepage.com/Racer_1_Forum.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorob.homepage.com/Racer_1_Forum.html</A> <P>The webpage looks weak but I gut a pick of my on-road HPI car while I was racing it.||||reg||14
Z||000007||DJRice||10-01-1999||09:07 AM||||Hey sniper, My first real R/C was a double dare!  I found it at a Sears Outlet Store for about $120 almost 10 years ago and I still have it.  That thing was a dog bone eater.  I never wanted to spend the extra money for the metal dog bone kit.<P>I have a Team Losi XXT cr now that I bought to race with some friends, but I moved away and havent touched it in a while.||||reg||1
