Z||000011||BlackGT||02-20-2000||11:34 PM||||Damn,<BR>And I thought I was the only one on this forum who raced R/C cars! I never came across<BR>this post on the board but I would be willing to buy 5 of those bodies...in fact<BR>I`ll contact Bolink myself, they`re just up the road from me in Georgia. BTW I am the ROAR Region 3 Gas-On Road 2WD Champ as well<BR>as The Champ for 2WD Gas-On road with the Dixie Race Club in Atlanta! I love those 1/10th scale missles. I`m forming a 1/10th scale drag club here in Atlanta this spring.<BR>Get gas or Go home!||||reg||6
Z||000012||fierospeeder||02-21-2000||12:11 AM||||Ive never raced them but i own three.  RC 10, a clod buster, had a lady drag it with her car when i accidently got it on the street, i have to rebuild it.  Also a kysho USA 1 truck, i havn't finished.  I got 2 planes, one trainer, and a piper cub i havn't finished.  I spend money on cars and i dont have time to do my rc hobby, its been years.  I might do the airplane again this summer, i have to try solo this time, i had an instructor few years ago, helping me fly.<P>Greendano.  I was wondering on your USA truck, the electric one, what servo are you using for the steering, i have probs because it seems it doesn't turn the wheels enough and the inside rims would get scratched by the plastic bars front and back where that servo rod is used to turn both at the same time and they are connected by tie rods to the wheels. Also is there a screw thats suppose to be on that plastic bar which is shown in the manual?||||reg||1
